{
  "scene1": {
    "scene": "scene1",
    "audio_file": "scene1_audio.mp3",
    "total_duration": 31.056,
    "sentences": [
      {
        "beat_index": 1,
        "text": "Imagine you throw a cricket ball straight up into the air.",
        "is_optional": false,
        "start": 0.0,
        "end": 3.336,
        "duration": 3.336,
        "file": "scene1_beat_01.mp3"
      },
      {
        "beat_index": 2,
        "text": "How high is it after one second?",
        "is_optional": false,
        "start": 3.636,
        "end": 5.94,
        "duration": 2.304,
        "file": "scene1_beat_02.mp3"
      },
      {
        "beat_index": 3,
        "text": "After two seconds?",
        "is_optional": false,
        "start": 6.24,
        "end": 8.112,
        "duration": 1.872,
        "file": "scene1_beat_03.mp3"
      },
      {
        "beat_index": 4,
        "text": "And when does it come back down?",
        "is_optional": false,
        "start": 8.412,
        "end": 10.524,
        "duration": 2.112,
        "file": "scene1_beat_04.mp3"
      },
      {
        "beat_index": 5,
        "text": "These questions have exact answers, and the tool that gives them is called a function.",
        "is_optional": false,
        "start": 10.824,
        "end": 15.504,
        "duration": 4.68,
        "file": "scene1_beat_05.mp3"
      },
      {
        "beat_index": 6,
        "text": "A function is a rule that takes an input, here the time, and gives back exactly one output, here the height.",
        "is_optional": false,
        "start": 15.804,
        "end": 21.948,
        "duration": 6.144,
        "file": "scene1_beat_06.mp3"
      },
      {
        "beat_index": 7,
        "text": "In this video, we will use this ball to understand three things: how inputs map to outputs, how to read a graph, and which key features tell the whole story.",
        "is_optional": false,
        "start": 22.248,
        "end": 30.72,
        "duration": 8.472,
        "file": "scene1_beat_07.mp3"
      }
    ]
  },
  "scene2": {
    "scene": "scene2",
    "audio_file": "scene2_audio.mp3",
    "total_duration": 60.312,
    "sentences": [
      {
        "beat_index": 1,
        "text": "Let's make this precise.",
        "is_optional": false,
        "start": 0.0,
        "end": 1.944,
        "duration": 1.944,
        "file": "scene2_beat_01.mp3"
      },
      {
        "beat_index": 2,
        "text": "A function assigns to each allowed input exactly one output.",
        "is_optional": false,
        "start": 2.244,
        "end": 6.084,
        "duration": 3.84,
        "file": "scene2_beat_02.mp3"
      },
      {
        "beat_index": 3,
        "text": "Our input is the time, tee, in seconds.",
        "is_optional": false,
        "start": 6.384,
        "end": 9.288,
        "duration": 2.904,
        "file": "scene2_beat_03.mp3"
      },
      {
        "beat_index": 4,
        "text": "Our output is the height, aitch of tee, in metres.",
        "is_optional": false,
        "start": 9.588,
        "end": 12.9,
        "duration": 3.312,
        "file": "scene2_beat_04.mp3"
      },
      {
        "beat_index": 5,
        "text": "If the ball is thrown upward at twenty metres per second, and we ignore air resistance, physics gives the rule: aitch of tee equals twenty tee minus five tee squared.",
        "is_optional": false,
        "start": 13.2,
        "end": 21.72,
        "duration": 8.52,
        "file": "scene2_beat_05.mp3"
      },
      {
        "beat_index": 6,
        "text": "Here we take gravity as ten metres per second squared, to keep the numbers clean.",
        "is_optional": false,
        "start": 22.02,
        "end": 26.748,
        "duration": 4.728,
        "file": "scene2_beat_06.mp3"
      },
      {
        "beat_index": 7,
        "text": "Let's test the rule.",
        "is_optional": false,
        "start": 27.048,
        "end": 28.92,
        "duration": 1.872,
        "file": "scene2_beat_07.mp3"
      },
      {
        "beat_index": 8,
        "text": "At tee equals one, we get twenty minus five, which is fifteen metres.",
        "is_optional": false,
        "start": 29.22,
        "end": 33.66,
        "duration": 4.44,
        "file": "scene2_beat_08.mp3"
      },
      {
        "beat_index": 9,
        "text": "Here is the full mapping.",
        "is_optional": false,
        "start": 33.96,
        "end": 35.952,
        "duration": 1.992,
        "file": "scene2_beat_09.mp3"
      },
      {
        "beat_index": 10,
        "text": "Zero goes to zero.",
        "is_optional": false,
        "start": 36.252,
        "end": 38.148,
        "duration": 1.896,
        "file": "scene2_beat_10.mp3"
      },
      {
        "beat_index": 11,
        "text": "One goes to fifteen.",
        "is_optional": false,
        "start": 38.448,
        "end": 40.344,
        "duration": 1.896,
        "file": "scene2_beat_11.mp3"
      },
      {
        "beat_index": 12,
        "text": "Two goes to twenty.",
        "is_optional": false,
        "start": 40.644,
        "end": 42.516,
        "duration": 1.872,
        "file": "scene2_beat_12.mp3"
      },
      {
        "beat_index": 13,
        "text": "Three goes to fifteen.",
        "is_optional": false,
        "start": 42.816,
        "end": 44.688,
        "duration": 1.872,
        "file": "scene2_beat_13.mp3"
      },
      {
        "beat_index": 14,
        "text": "And four goes to zero.",
        "is_optional": false,
        "start": 44.988,
        "end": 46.884,
        "duration": 1.896,
        "file": "scene2_beat_14.mp3"
      },
      {
        "beat_index": 15,
        "text": "Notice that every input has exactly one arrow leaving it.",
        "is_optional": false,
        "start": 47.184,
        "end": 50.832,
        "duration": 3.648,
        "file": "scene2_beat_15.mp3"
      },
      {
        "beat_index": 16,
        "text": "That is what makes it a function.",
        "is_optional": false,
        "start": 51.132,
        "end": 53.436,
        "duration": 2.304,
        "file": "scene2_beat_16.mp3"
      },
      {
        "beat_index": 17,
        "text": "The set of allowed inputs is the domain, and the set of outputs the function actually produces is the range.",
        "is_optional": false,
        "start": 53.736,
        "end": 59.376,
        "duration": 5.64,
        "file": "scene2_beat_17.mp3"
      }
    ]
  },
  "scene3": {
    "scene": "scene3",
    "audio_file": "scene3_audio.mp3",
    "total_duration": 63.288,
    "sentences": [
      {
        "beat_index": 1,
        "text": "Now let's turn this mapping into a graph.",
        "is_optional": false,
        "start": 0.0,
        "end": 2.616,
        "duration": 2.616,
        "file": "scene3_beat_01.mp3"
      },
      {
        "beat_index": 2,
        "text": "Each input-output pair becomes a point: time goes on the horizontal axis, and height goes on the vertical axis.",
        "is_optional": false,
        "start": 2.916,
        "end": 9.324,
        "duration": 6.408,
        "file": "scene3_beat_02.mp3"
      },
      {
        "beat_index": 3,
        "text": "Zero comma zero.",
        "is_optional": false,
        "start": 9.624,
        "end": 11.496,
        "duration": 1.872,
        "file": "scene3_beat_03.mp3"
      },
      {
        "beat_index": 4,
        "text": "One comma fifteen.",
        "is_optional": false,
        "start": 11.796,
        "end": 13.668,
        "duration": 1.872,
        "file": "scene3_beat_04.mp3"
      },
      {
        "beat_index": 5,
        "text": "Two comma twenty.",
        "is_optional": false,
        "start": 13.968,
        "end": 15.84,
        "duration": 1.872,
        "file": "scene3_beat_05.mp3"
      },
      {
        "beat_index": 6,
        "text": "Three comma fifteen.",
        "is_optional": false,
        "start": 16.14,
        "end": 18.012,
        "duration": 1.872,
        "file": "scene3_beat_06.mp3"
      },
      {
        "beat_index": 7,
        "text": "Four comma zero.",
        "is_optional": false,
        "start": 18.312,
        "end": 20.184,
        "duration": 1.872,
        "file": "scene3_beat_07.mp3"
      },
      {
        "beat_index": 8,
        "text": "Join the points smoothly, and we get a curve called a parabola.",
        "is_optional": false,
        "start": 20.484,
        "end": 24.3,
        "duration": 3.816,
        "file": "scene3_beat_08.mp3"
      },
      {
        "beat_index": 9,
        "text": "It rises, peaks, and falls symmetrically.",
        "is_optional": false,
        "start": 24.6,
        "end": 27.768,
        "duration": 3.168,
        "file": "scene3_beat_09.mp3"
      },
      {
        "beat_index": 10,
        "text": "Be careful: this is not the path of the ball in space, because the ball moves straight up and down.",
        "is_optional": false,
        "start": 28.068,
        "end": 33.708,
        "duration": 5.64,
        "file": "scene3_beat_10.mp3"
      },
      {
        "beat_index": 11,
        "text": "The graph shows height against time.",
        "is_optional": false,
        "start": 34.008,
        "end": 36.384,
        "duration": 2.376,
        "file": "scene3_beat_11.mp3"
      },
      {
        "beat_index": 12,
        "text": "Notice also that at one second and at three seconds the height is the same, fifteen metres.",
        "is_optional": false,
        "start": 36.684,
        "end": 41.628,
        "duration": 4.944,
        "file": "scene3_beat_12.mp3"
      },
      {
        "beat_index": 13,
        "text": "Two different inputs may share an output.",
        "is_optional": false,
        "start": 41.928,
        "end": 44.448,
        "duration": 2.52,
        "file": "scene3_beat_13.mp3"
      },
      {
        "beat_index": 14,
        "text": "But one input can never have two outputs, because at any moment the ball has only one height.",
        "is_optional": false,
        "start": 44.748,
        "end": 50.052,
        "duration": 5.304,
        "file": "scene3_beat_14.mp3"
      },
      {
        "beat_index": 15,
        "text": "That gives us the vertical line test: if every vertical line crosses a graph at most once, the graph shows a function.",
        "is_optional": false,
        "start": 50.352,
        "end": 57.024,
        "duration": 6.672,
        "file": "scene3_beat_15.mp3"
      },
      {
        "beat_index": 16,
        "text": "A circle fails this test, because the line at ex equals zero crosses it twice.",
        "is_optional": false,
        "start": 57.324,
        "end": 62.412,
        "duration": 5.088,
        "file": "scene3_beat_16.mp3"
      }
    ]
  },
  "scene4": {
    "scene": "scene4",
    "audio_file": "scene4_audio.mp3",
    "total_duration": 93.0,
    "sentences": [
      {
        "beat_index": 1,
        "text": "Now let's find the key features step by step.",
        "is_optional": false,
        "start": 0.0,
        "end": 2.928,
        "duration": 2.928,
        "file": "scene4_beat_01.mp3"
      },
      {
        "beat_index": 2,
        "text": "First, the intercepts.",
        "is_optional": false,
        "start": 3.228,
        "end": 5.268,
        "duration": 2.04,
        "file": "scene4_beat_02.mp3"
      },
      {
        "beat_index": 3,
        "text": "At tee equals zero, aitch is zero, so the graph starts at the origin.",
        "is_optional": false,
        "start": 5.568,
        "end": 10.032,
        "duration": 4.464,
        "file": "scene4_beat_03.mp3"
      },
      {
        "beat_index": 4,
        "text": "To find when the ball lands, set aitch equal to zero: twenty tee minus five tee squared equals zero.",
        "is_optional": false,
        "start": 10.332,
        "end": 16.284,
        "duration": 5.952,
        "file": "scene4_beat_04.mp3"
      },
      {
        "beat_index": 5,
        "text": "Factorising, five tee times, four minus tee, equals zero.",
        "is_optional": false,
        "start": 16.584,
        "end": 20.904,
        "duration": 4.32,
        "file": "scene4_beat_05.mp3"
      },
      {
        "beat_index": 6,
        "text": "So tee is zero or tee is four.",
        "is_optional": false,
        "start": 21.204,
        "end": 23.676,
        "duration": 2.472,
        "file": "scene4_beat_06.mp3"
      },
      {
        "beat_index": 7,
        "text": "The ball lands after four seconds.",
        "is_optional": false,
        "start": 23.976,
        "end": 26.376,
        "duration": 2.4,
        "file": "scene4_beat_07.mp3"
      },
      {
        "beat_index": 8,
        "text": "Second, the highest point.",
        "is_optional": false,
        "start": 26.676,
        "end": 28.932,
        "duration": 2.256,
        "file": "scene4_beat_08.mp3"
      },
      {
        "beat_index": 9,
        "text": "We can rewrite the rule as twenty minus five times, tee minus two, squared.",
        "is_optional": false,
        "start": 29.232,
        "end": 33.912,
        "duration": 4.68,
        "file": "scene4_beat_09.mp3"
      },
      {
        "beat_index": 10,
        "text": "The squared term is never negative, so the height is largest when it is zero, at tee equals two.",
        "is_optional": false,
        "start": 34.212,
        "end": 39.42,
        "duration": 5.208,
        "file": "scene4_beat_10.mp3"
      },
      {
        "beat_index": 11,
        "text": "There, aitch equals twenty.",
        "is_optional": false,
        "start": 39.72,
        "end": 42.0,
        "duration": 2.28,
        "file": "scene4_beat_11.mp3"
      },
      {
        "beat_index": 12,
        "text": "The maximum height is twenty metres, after two seconds.",
        "is_optional": false,
        "start": 42.3,
        "end": 45.684,
        "duration": 3.384,
        "file": "scene4_beat_12.mp3"
      },
      {
        "beat_index": 13,
        "text": "Third, the domain and range.",
        "is_optional": false,
        "start": 45.984,
        "end": 48.192,
        "duration": 2.208,
        "file": "scene4_beat_13.mp3"
      },
      {
        "beat_index": 14,
        "text": "The formula accepts any real number, but the ball only flies from zero to four seconds, so the domain here is zero to four.",
        "is_optional": false,
        "start": 48.492,
        "end": 55.404,
        "duration": 6.912,
        "file": "scene4_beat_14.mp3"
      },
      {
        "beat_index": 15,
        "text": "The height stays between zero and twenty, so the range is zero to twenty.",
        "is_optional": false,
        "start": 55.704,
        "end": 59.928,
        "duration": 4.224,
        "file": "scene4_beat_15.mp3"
      },
      {
        "beat_index": 16,
        "text": "Finally, the behaviour.",
        "is_optional": false,
        "start": 60.228,
        "end": 62.34,
        "duration": 2.112,
        "file": "scene4_beat_16.mp3"
      },
      {
        "beat_index": 17,
        "text": "From zero to two seconds the graph is increasing.",
        "is_optional": false,
        "start": 62.64,
        "end": 65.712,
        "duration": 3.072,
        "file": "scene4_beat_17.mp3"
      },
      {
        "beat_index": 18,
        "text": "From two to four it is decreasing.",
        "is_optional": false,
        "start": 66.012,
        "end": 68.364,
        "duration": 2.352,
        "file": "scene4_beat_18.mp3"
      },
      {
        "beat_index": 19,
        "text": "To measure how fast, look at the average change in height per second.",
        "is_optional": false,
        "start": 68.664,
        "end": 72.672,
        "duration": 4.008,
        "file": "scene4_beat_19.mp3"
      },
      {
        "beat_index": 20,
        "text": "From zero to one: fifteen.",
        "is_optional": false,
        "start": 72.972,
        "end": 75.444,
        "duration": 2.472,
        "file": "scene4_beat_20.mp3"
      },
      {
        "beat_index": 21,
        "text": "From one to two: five.",
        "is_optional": false,
        "start": 75.744,
        "end": 77.88,
        "duration": 2.136,
        "file": "scene4_beat_21.mp3"
      },
      {
        "beat_index": 22,
        "text": "From two to three: minus five.",
        "is_optional": false,
        "start": 78.18,
        "end": 80.724,
        "duration": 2.544,
        "file": "scene4_beat_22.mp3"
      },
      {
        "beat_index": 23,
        "text": "From three to four: minus fifteen.",
        "is_optional": false,
        "start": 81.024,
        "end": 83.76,
        "duration": 2.736,
        "file": "scene4_beat_23.mp3"
      },
      {
        "beat_index": 24,
        "text": "A negative value means the ball is moving downward.",
        "is_optional": false,
        "start": 84.06,
        "end": 87.204,
        "duration": 3.144,
        "file": "scene4_beat_24.mp3"
      },
      {
        "beat_index": 25,
        "text": "The climb slows down, stops at the peak, and the fall speeds up.",
        "is_optional": false,
        "start": 87.504,
        "end": 91.584,
        "duration": 4.08,
        "file": "scene4_beat_25.mp3"
      }
    ]
  },
  "scene5": {
    "scene": "scene5",
    "audio_file": "scene5_audio.mp3",
    "total_duration": 35.832,
    "sentences": [
      {
        "beat_index": 1,
        "text": "Now let's read the graph as a story.",
        "is_optional": false,
        "start": 0.0,
        "end": 2.568,
        "duration": 2.568,
        "file": "scene5_beat_01.mp3"
      },
      {
        "beat_index": 2,
        "text": "The starting point says: the ball leaves your hand at height zero.",
        "is_optional": false,
        "start": 2.868,
        "end": 6.612,
        "duration": 3.744,
        "file": "scene5_beat_02.mp3"
      },
      {
        "beat_index": 3,
        "text": "The peak says: for an instant, at two seconds, the ball is twenty metres up and stops rising.",
        "is_optional": false,
        "start": 6.912,
        "end": 12.504,
        "duration": 5.592,
        "file": "scene5_beat_03.mp3"
      },
      {
        "beat_index": 4,
        "text": "The second intercept says: it lands after four seconds.",
        "is_optional": false,
        "start": 12.804,
        "end": 16.284,
        "duration": 3.48,
        "file": "scene5_beat_04.mp3"
      },
      {
        "beat_index": 5,
        "text": "The symmetry says: it takes exactly as long to fall as to rise.",
        "is_optional": false,
        "start": 16.584,
        "end": 20.976,
        "duration": 4.392,
        "file": "scene5_beat_05.mp3"
      },
      {
        "beat_index": 6,
        "text": "And the domain reminds us that this formula describes the ball only between zero and four seconds.",
        "is_optional": false,
        "start": 21.276,
        "end": 26.676,
        "duration": 5.4,
        "file": "scene5_beat_06.mp3"
      },
      {
        "beat_index": 7,
        "text": "Before the throw, or after the landing, it says nothing useful.",
        "is_optional": false,
        "start": 26.976,
        "end": 30.864,
        "duration": 3.888,
        "file": "scene5_beat_07.mp3"
      },
      {
        "beat_index": 8,
        "text": "That is the power of a graph: it shows a whole relationship at a glance.",
        "is_optional": false,
        "start": 31.164,
        "end": 35.436,
        "duration": 4.272,
        "file": "scene5_beat_08.mp3"
      }
    ]
  },
  "scene6": {
    "scene": "scene6",
    "audio_file": "scene6_audio.mp3",
    "total_duration": 27.456,
    "sentences": [
      {
        "beat_index": 1,
        "text": "Let's recap three ideas.",
        "is_optional": false,
        "start": 0.0,
        "end": 2.184,
        "duration": 2.184,
        "file": "scene6_beat_01.mp3"
      },
      {
        "beat_index": 2,
        "text": "One: a function gives each input exactly one output, and the vertical line test checks this on a graph.",
        "is_optional": false,
        "start": 2.484,
        "end": 8.484,
        "duration": 6.0,
        "file": "scene6_beat_02.mp3"
      },
      {
        "beat_index": 3,
        "text": "Two: on a graph, each point is an input-output pair, with the input on the horizontal axis.",
        "is_optional": false,
        "start": 8.784,
        "end": 14.544,
        "duration": 5.76,
        "file": "scene6_beat_03.mp3"
      },
      {
        "beat_index": 4,
        "text": "Three: the intercepts, the maximum, the domain and range, and where the graph rises or falls, tell the real-life story.",
        "is_optional": false,
        "start": 14.844,
        "end": 21.564,
        "duration": 6.72,
        "file": "scene6_beat_04.mp3"
      },
      {
        "beat_index": 5,
        "text": "Thanks for watching.",
        "is_optional": false,
        "start": 21.864,
        "end": 23.736,
        "duration": 1.872,
        "file": "scene6_beat_05.mp3"
      },
      {
        "beat_index": 6,
        "text": "Credits and the AI disclosure are on screen.",
        "is_optional": false,
        "start": 24.036,
        "end": 27.18,
        "duration": 3.144,
        "file": "scene6_beat_06.mp3"
      }
    ]
  },
